# A public member added to class C changes the API of trait T extending it (inherited members
# are part of T's API), so T and D are recompiled in the second round as descendants of C, and
# no third round follows. T's extraHash folds in only trait parents, so the change to C is not
# also reported as a change to T's private members.
> compile
$ copy-file changes/C1.scala C.scala
> compile
> checkIterations 3
> checkRecompilations 1 C
> checkRecompilations 2 T D
